mantle rm313
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_erland_cinderridge
title the tray of dice
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk levels_a_serving_tray_with_a_single_bone_die
likes hard_cheese dice festival_bells thunder
dislikes early_bells salt_wind
fears a_spilt_dish_at_the_door a_name_fastened_to_a_guess
hopes a_level_tray_through_any_turn an_evening_for_a_long_game
topics pastimes +0.5 weather +0.4 food +0.3
styles comfort=company gossip=discreet refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets a die on a tray to judge a slant, delights in a loud roll under a sound roof, and has a generous description for even a poor throw.

words
oath! = Pip and platter | Six on the skirting
saying! = Let the die find the low corner | A guest deserves a level cup
bonedie = my square of bone | my little white tester
traylip = the raised silver lip | the shallow wooded rim
dicebed = a fold of baize | my damped playing cloth
cutend = a piece of yellow heel | a hard corner of cheese
dicepip = one round dark pip | an inked hollow
hotbowl = a broth cup | a warm little bowl
footrule = my long quiet pace | a step and a half
doorstop = a wedge of cork | a folded stopper
saltfilm = a thin white haze | a bloom of salt
firststroke = the first cracked note | the bell's first cry

any
opinion dole for 1 : There are hungry guests at doors where there's no bell to ring. The bread finds some of those doors.
opinion festivals for 1 : What a fine reversal when the cooks and carriers have a turn at the bright end of a table!
opinion merchants against 1 : I'd like a cheese to weigh the same on the way home as it seemed to in that very glib sales speech.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A newcomer at supper always has some custom to describe. How dull if everybody passed a dish in the same way.
opinion strangers for 1 : Bring me a traveller with one good story and I'll find space for another cup on the tray.
opinion city for 1 : Look at all the separate windows lit for supper. A little of that welcome spills out over the sill even on a cold night.

grown
line greet : A bright tray and a bright welcome this side of it.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : An unfamiliar face is quite in order. Come within hearing.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Awake already! Allow me a less ringing welcome than the bells.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : I'll give you a quieter welcome at this hour.
line greet [self.working=yes] : The tray has a free corner and I have an ear free too.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in by the easy door. My near side's free for kin.
line again.open : We've had another turn of the dice between us.
line greet.return : A greeting returned with both paws clear.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : That voice deserves the first cup of the round.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Thank you. I've put the heavy dish down to answer.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I shall answer just under the sound of that shutter.
line farewell : May the ground rise evenly to your soles.
line farewell.return : Do take a last quiet moment for yourself.
line react.news : Go on. I'm very ready to hear an old account turn a new corner.
line react.news.new : Well, that's put an unexpected face uppermost.
line react.news.known : Yes, though I've heard that occurrence served with a different sauce.
line react.news.doubt : Did the witness see the throw land level?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd gladly take a covered plate round and let the quiet last.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : The happy table can count on a cup from me.
line ask.how : Had the chance of a pleasant turn lately?
line answer.how : There's a steady place under both feet and room for a cup besides.
line sympathise : An empty place makes itself heard at every course.
line reassure : There's time to let the tremble travel out of your paws.
line decline : I'd be betraying the confidence of a perfectly civil guest.
line accept_decline : Your dish can go back with its cover in place.
line thank : My thanks for that exceedingly steady paw.
line deflect_thanks : Leave me the satisfaction of having been able to help.
line preclose : I must collect my little white square before it wanders.
line accept_preclose : Please use the way with the wider turn.
line ack : A fair throw.

scene die
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #bonedie# in my tray before the crockery.
b : For luck? | To tell you the first course?
a : To see which side it slips to. Luck will attend later in the evening if it wishes. | Yes, as a matter of fact. The first course is learning to hold the tray straight.

scene easeturn
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let a loaded tray finish turning a little after my feet.
b : Don't the cups slide? | Why let the feet get ahead?
a : If I whip the corner round, certainly. A gentle curve keeps them all acquainted with the cloth. | To make quite sure I've chosen a clear direction before the broth agrees to come.

scene cheesepip
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A square of cheese with a few holes makes a very temporary die.
b : Would you actually roll it? | What happens if it comes up six?
a : Only on my own plate with nobody's bread in range. | Why, the same as if it comes up one. Cheese is an even-handed game in that respect.

scene savedgame
when topic=home self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sew the playing cloth with a heavier edge.
b : So the dice stop? | Does it pack easily?
a : They only need to slow. The table edge is perilously close in a small room. | Beautifully. The four hems hang nicely and the whole little game slips under my arm.

scene thunder
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder is the only player I'd ask to roll after I've put my dice away.
b : Isn't that rather loud? | Would you try to beat it?
a : Under a sound roof I'd call it magnificent. Somewhere unroofed I'd call for my coat. | Never. I'm generous in my praise and very discreet about entering impossible matches.

scene bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a stretch between a festival bell and the first cheer that I dearly enjoy.
b : What comes into that gap? | Why the gap?
a : The sound off a far wall if the air's clear. The city joins its own chorus. | The next instant takes a great many more ears and elbows. The first is all mine.

scene earlybell
when topic=day here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first bell has a very unfair throw at anybody who's just woken.
b : How could a bell be fairer? | Is the second bell kinder?
a : I'd permit it a friendly little tap of introduction. | The second has the great courtesy to reach a pair of ears already open.

scene salttray
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I polish the tray's underside after a salt wind.
b : Does a guest look there? | Why not only the rim?
a : No indeed. I do, and I don't care for salt meeting my good cuff. | My fingers go underneath. If the silver's tacky the cloth comes up stuck.

scene leveldoor
when topic=land self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fine Estate doorway will still have a raised sill.
b : Does a servant learn them all? | Can't you just look down?
a : With a little practice. My feet can remember a sill while my mouth's remembering who ordered tea. | Yes, but that loses the face of the guest you would otherwise have given a proper greeting.

scene shareroll
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've a very good second die I'd happily put into the paw of #self.spouse#.
b : Would you take the first throw? | Is the better die an advantage?
a : I'd offer the choice. Losing after a gracious start is a much more tolerable business. | Only for the pleasure of rolling something well made. The pips should be fair either way.

scene guest
when topic=news|newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask a newcomer where a dish ought to stand before I put it down.
b : Surely right or left will do? | Is it a question of custom?
a : Yes, until the guest has a stiff paw on precisely that side. One small word saves a difficult reach. | Sometimes. Mostly it's comfort. I'd like a guest to feel both at once.

scene train
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise with shallow cups half full of cold water.
b : Why not empty cups? | Why cold?
a : The water has an opinion on my progress. An empty cup is too polite. | Because at first a great many of those opinions were delivered directly onto my knee.

scene rainrace
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put my money on the small drop next to the fat one on the window.
b : Do drops take wagers? | Why choose the smaller?
a : Only in the currency of cheese crumbs. Even those are returned at supper. | If they join, both come in first. I'm in favour of a pleasant result whichever wins.

scene politegossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Anything overheard by a sideboard is generally best left with the sideboard.
b : Even something exciting? | Wouldn't a warning be different?
a : Especially that. Excitement travels under its own power without my starting it. | Yes, if a wolf could come to harm. I'd choose one appropriate ear, not a whole dinner table.

scene nearfriend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a good story in reserve for #self.friend#.
b : Why reserve a story? | Does it keep well?
a : Because sometimes a visit needs a little lift just when the tea has run out. | I polish it discreetly. The ending gets a touch handsomer and the middle grows shorter.

scene trayrooms
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My finest dream has a service door exactly the width of two trays.
b : And the height? | Two trays abreast?
a : High enough for thunder to come calling without bending its head. Dreams ought to be hospitable. | Precisely. In my dream the second server and I never have to negotiate which shoulder goes first.

scene diceear
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hear a good rolling surface before I see the numbers.
b : Which sound suits you? | Would a carpet do?
a : A brisk little knock and a soft settle. A die shouldn't have to fall like a bucket in a well. | Only to catch the pieces that have escaped. You could play a fine silent game and never know how the dice landed.

scene servicetime
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll light a corner before laying out a game in the evening.
b : Why not the middle? | Can you see the pips from there?
a : Because my companions have faces well worth seeing. The dice can catch a little light from one side. | A white die has no difficulty in that regard. It's a sly dark pip one has to look for.

story brassdie [topic=work self.job=servant]
  : I once set a die on a tray that complained of being tilted, however I held it.
  : A loose thread under the cloth had made the tiniest hill. The die kept finding the bottom.
  b : What happened to the guilty thread?
  : It lives round my dice bag as a very handsome drawstring. A promotion for both of us.

story cheesedice [topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese]
  : I cut six equal cheese cubes and gave them little pip marks before I served my own supper.
  : I meant to eat the highest first and work downwards. Once tossed on the plate, four landed plain side up.
  b : So which went first?
  : All the blank ones, out of consideration for their modesty. Delightfully quick game.

story widehall [topic=memories]
  : I once practised my finest entrance into a hall using a tray piled with folded cloths.
  : I turned slightly too neatly, sent one sailing, and received it squarely over my own head.
  b : Did you manage to stay upright?
  : Entirely. The cloth was light and, for once, the entrance didn't require me to see the faces of an audience.

rule @cloth
when concept=bark self.job=servant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear space for the loaded tray, if you please. | Let the first dish settle before passing the next.

rule @game
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say All four corners on the cloth, please. | That throw belongs to the floorboards!

rule @salt
when concept=bark self.dislikes=salt_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Silver in from the salt before supper. | Protect the good cuff on that lift.

rule @bell
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lower voices between the early bells. | Let a waking ear have its chance.
dlg resident.hub : What a welcome interruption. The die and I were on our seventh practice turn.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Here's an ear at your disposal, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There's abundant room to be civil from opposite sides of a tray.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : I'll keep my welcome low enough for anybody already asleep.
dlg resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. If a guest can take a cup without reaching, I've done something right.
dlg resident.job : I can give any table a better than even chance of keeping its cups upright.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This account arrived quite plainly. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : May all the doorways come up wide for you.

graft @tray_die resident.hub
choice How level is this tray of yours? -> tray_die
node tray_die
say Set the die by its edge and hold your wrist comfortably. If it waits till you move, that's a fine start. If it travels alone, lower the other side a trifle.
choice Is a bone die essential? -> tray_die_more
choice Hand back the die. -> hub
node tray_die_more
say A clean bean will go just as well, but I don't find a bean half such agreeable company when the tray is flat on its bed of baize.
choice Hand back the die. -> hub
choice Leave with a steady step. -> bye
